# 17. Now evolution begins

This is where three other papers become relevant.

They are **not additional benchmark architectures**.

They tell us how to search beyond the ten.

## GPTSwarm

arXiv:2402.16823 represents agents as computational graphs and optimizes node prompts and graph connectivity. ([arXiv][13])

## AFlow

arXiv:2410.10762 represents workflows as code graphs and uses an MCTS-like optimizer over operators such as Generate, Review, Revise and Ensemble. ([arXiv][14])

## ADAS

arXiv:2408.08435 allows a meta-agent to generate entirely new agent implementations based on an archive of previous discoveries. ([arXiv][15])

Therefore CoGym's evolution layer should combine the useful parts:

```text
GPTSwarm
graph representation

+

AFlow
structured mutation operators/search

+

ADAS
LLM-generated novel architectures

+

CoGym
sealed deterministic evaluation
```

That's a very compelling lineage.

