# 30. The four findings I'd aim to discover

Don't predetermine them, but these would make exceptionally strong experimental outcomes:

**Finding 1 — Independent reasoning beats conversation.**

```text
parallel proposals > shared group chat
```

because shared chat causes correlated errors/herding.

**Finding 2 — More reasoning has diminishing returns.**

```text
one critic round good
three debate rounds bad
```

**Finding 3 — Raw memory hurts under regime change.**

```text
validated + recency-aware memory
>
retrieve-everything memory
```

**Finding 4 — Dynamic orchestration preserves quality at much lower cost.**

```text
conditional specialists
≈ full committee quality

but

40–60% fewer calls
```

Even if only one or two emerge, that's already a meaningful contribution.

