# 31. Canonical scope

I would explicitly **not** spend this week on:

```text
RL weight training
fine-tuning
complex strategy discovery
hundreds of financial indicators
live execution
massive web-news pipelines
social-agent economies
arbitrary agent-generated Python
```

The interesting object is:

> **architecture effectiveness under controlled uncertainty.**

Then once the architecture is scientifically established, CoGym can later become a general-purpose reasoning laboratory for other worlds as originally intended.

The clean architecture is therefore:

```text
                 COGYM

         10 literature seeds
                  │
                  ▼
       common ArchitectureGenome
                  │
                  ▼
      deterministic experiments
                  │
                  ▼
          FINSABER replay
                  │
                  ▼
       validated experiment graph
                  │
               HydraDB
                  │
                  ▼
       architecture evolution
     GPTSwarm/AFlow/ADAS-inspired
                  │
                  ▼
            sealed holdout
                  │
                  ▼
          frozen champion
                  │
                  ▼
        Alpaca paper demonstration
```

**That is the development plan I'd make canonical.** The biggest immediate engineering work is not the Alpaca connection; it's building `ArchitectureGenome + ArchitectureExecutor + ten seed adapters + FINSABER adapter`. Once those exist, your existing CoGym evaluation/evolution infrastructure can do most of the interesting work.

